        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #6671 \u2014 weather widget showing \"No integration data available\" despite being configured.\n\n## Root cause\n\nSince the v1.75.0 refactor, `widget.weather.atLocation` returns `null` when the `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION` env flag is set, but `location.searchCity` (the city picker in the widget settings) was never guarded. A user with `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION=true` can search and select a city, yet every weather widget shows \"No integration data available\" \u2014 exactly the reported symptom. Before 1.75.0 there was no guard at all, which matches \"worked in earlier versions\".\n\n## Changes\n\n- `packages/api/src/router/location.ts` \u2014 `location.searchCity` now respects `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION` and returns `{ results: [] }` without making an outbound request, consistent with weather/RSS/analytics routers.\n- `packages/widgets/src/weather/component.tsx` \u2014 distinguishes query states:\n  - loading \u2192 empty state (unchanged)\n  - error \u2192 \"Failed to load weather data\" + Retry button\n  - `null` (external connections disabled) \u2192 explicit \"Weather data is unavailable because outbound connections are disabled\"\n- `packages/translation/src/lang/en.json` \u2014 new `widget.weather.error.{disabled,failed,retry}` keys\n- Docs: weather widget page and `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION` env-var page now mention location search is also disabled.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded `packages/api/src/router/test/location.spec.ts` and `packages/api/src/router/test/widgets/weather.spec.ts` covering both flag states. Verified: affected vitest suites (62 tests), `tsc --noEmit` for api + widgets, `oxlint`, `oxfmt`.\n\n## Verification\n\nBooted the published `v1.76.0` image with `DB_DIALECT=sqlite`:\n- with `NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION=true`: `atLocation` \u2192 `null`, `searchCity` \u2192 results (bug)\n- without the flag: both endpoints return data\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added clear weather widget states for loading failures and unavailable data.\n  - Added a retry action when weather data cannot be loaded.\n  - Added localized messages for connection-disabled, loading-error, and retry scenarios.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - City search and weather requests now avoid external services when external connections are disabled.\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Updated environment variable and weather widget documentation to explain offline behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
