    "updated_at": "2026-08-23T00:47:56Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the quick fix - interesting behavior - I looked back in my git history and I've had NO_EXTERNAL_CONNECTION enabled since April, but I could have sworn the weather widget worked after that.  I could be mistaken though.\n\nSo I was still getting the same widget behavior until I removed and re-added it.  Now I get no messages within the settings at all (just no results when searching a city, Paris coordinates remain but the city I searched is now in that city/postal code field), but I do see a new message once I save: \"Weather data is unavailable because outbound connections are disabled\" so that is helpful.\n\nI'll have to look into why I set that env variable in the first place.\n\nMy first bug report but wanted to just say thanks for all the great work on this project!  I use this every day as my portal to all my services.  Plus the releases widget is the best implementation I've come across to monitor for updates.",
